  "writing_rules": [
    "All exact named teams use this representation regardless of narrative function.",
    "The runtime uses one generic team-training model; doctrine, instructors, facilities, membership, authority and classification are data.",
    "Every member_ref is a persistent exact person; aggregate formations use the formation model instead.",
    "leader_ref and deputy_ref, when present, must be members.",
    "Every exact team carries lifecycle state; standing and mission-bound purpose is explicit rather than inferred from record shape.",
    "Training instructors may be lawful external instructors and do not become team members merely by teaching; member_refs remains the roster authority.",
    "Standing teams persist across missions; mission_bound teams become dissolution-eligible only after their saved mission purpose is terminal.",
    "Active exact-team membership is exclusive for autonomous drafting; reorganization or lawful authority must release a member before another autonomous team may select them.",
    "Permanent losses may trigger lawful reconstitution according to replacement_policy; temporary injury, recovery, travel or capture does not silently erase membership.",
    "Do not add team-name-specific runtime fields or unregistered gameplay fields.",
    "current_assignment_ref is an operational overlay only; an exact team assigned to a formation is already included in that formation headcount.",
    "embedded_member_refs is the exact identity overlay currently counted inside current_assignment_ref; it is always a subset of member_refs and never changes formation headcount by itself.",
    "recent_sessions is a bounded mechanical ledger for schedule and recovery enforcement; semantic events keep long-form training history."
  ]
